Test PW DFT+U (U=5.0 eV, l=2) with collinear spin and fixed occupations.
The original three ionic steps, wavefunction cutoff (10 Ry), structure,
pseudopotential, orbital file, U value, and default Davidson-subspace solver
are retained. This checks a short relaxation trajectory, not a fully relaxed
structure.

The density cutoff is 160 Ry to resolve the charge and magnetic densities.
Real-space SCF convergence uses a normalized L1 residual below 1e-10,
including both spin channels. The magnetic mixing factor is 0.4; the charge
mixing factor remains 0.4. The electronic/diagonalization budgets are 200,
with an initial diagonalization threshold of 1e-13 and no empty-band
threshold smoothing.

These settings use the corrected dense-grid real-space mixing path: charge,
kinetic-density history, spin strides, Kerker FFTs, and the history inner
product all use the grid on which the real-space density is stored.
The previous implementation used the smaller smooth-grid size and failed
to mix the entire density when the grids differed.

The higher density cutoff also changes the short relaxation trajectory.
The former final energy was -5654.418683431447 eV; the recalculated
reference is approximately -5627.291202544 eV, a shift of about +27.13 eV.
The new reference is tied to the denser grid and the fully converged
electronic steps of the revised input.

Reference validation on 2026-10-28 used GNU 12.3, OpenMPI 5.0.10, CPU Release,
and one thread each for OpenMP, OpenBLAS and MKL. The reference comes from
an independent Davidson-subspace run. Davidson-subspace, Davidson and PPCG
were each rerun from clean inputs at 1, 2 and 4 MPI ranks. All nine runs
converged at all three ionic steps and passed the unchanged original
Autotest checks (36/36 properties), without PPCG residual warnings.

Across these nine runs, the final energy span was 4.232e-9 eV. The largest
force/stress component differences over every ionic step were 6.870e-8
eV/Angstrom and 1.710e-6 kbar. The original acceptance limits remain
1e-7 eV for energy, 1e-4 for the force aggregate, and 1e-3 for the stress
aggregate. The original reference remains in commit
77f7b4af69934064aa5f4b84267343e9135bc348.

To reproduce, use clean copies with ks_solver=dav_subspace, dav and ppcg,
and run the original tests/integrate/Autotest.sh at -n1, -n2 and -n4 with
-o1. Preserve all three ionic steps and the supplied fixed occ_mat.txt.
